{
  "title": "Burn down private helper imports in orchestrator modules",
  "description": "The orchestrator boundary is currently a façade over other modules' private helpers. `puppeteer/orchestrator.py` imports underscore-prefixed helpers from `batch_coordination`, `game_finalization`, `game_processes`, and `post_game_analysis`, then re-exports many of them via `__all__`. Tests and scripts now treat those internals as part of the orchestrator surface.\n\
\n\
Clean this up by making ownership explicit: callers should import the owning module directly, or the owning module should expose a deliberate public name. This issue should also cover the similar private imports already present in `batch_coordination.py` from `game_finalization.py` and `game_processes.py`.\n\
\n\
Scope:\n\
- `puppeteer/src/puppeteer/orchestrator.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/src/puppeteer/batch_coordination.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/src/puppeteer/game_finalization.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/src/puppeteer/game_processes.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/src/puppeteer/post_game_analysis.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/tests/test_orchestrator.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/tests/test_youtube.py`\n\
- `scripts/tournament_game.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/tests/test_weird_conventions.py` (remove the allowlist entries as debt is retired)",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "puppeteer",
    "python",
    "refactor",
  ],
